
== rounding to 0 places: halfeven awayfromzero tozero tonegativeinfinity topositiveinfinity ==
                even    away    zero    -inf    +inf
0.5                0       1       0       0       1
1.5                2       2       1       1       2
2.5                2       3       2       2       3
3.5                4       4       3       3       4
-0.5               0      -1       0      -1       0
-1.5              -2      -2      -1      -2      -1
-2.5              -2      -3      -2      -3      -2
2.4                2       2       2       2       3
2.6                3       3       2       2       3
-2.4              -2      -2      -2      -3      -2
-2.6              -3      -3      -2      -3      -2
2                  2       2       2       2       2

== rounding to 2 places ==
                even    away    zero    -inf    +inf
2.675           2.68    2.68    2.67    2.67    2.68
2.665           2.66    2.67    2.66    2.66    2.67
2.665001        2.67    2.67    2.66    2.66    2.67
2.664999        2.66    2.66    2.66    2.66    2.67
-2.675         -2.68   -2.68   -2.67   -2.68   -2.67
-2.665         -2.66   -2.67   -2.66   -2.67   -2.66
2.6              2.6     2.6     2.6     2.6     2.6
2.6000          2.60    2.60    2.60    2.60    2.60
0.005           0.00    0.01    0.00    0.00    0.01
0.015           0.02    0.02    0.01    0.01    0.02
0.025           0.02    0.03    0.02    0.02    0.03

== default is half-even (banker's rounding) ==
round(0.5d, 0)                     0
round(1.5d, 0)                     2
round(2.5d, 0)                     2
round(3.5d, 0)                     4
sum of 0.5 .. 99.5 (exact)         5000.0
sum of those rounded half-even     5000
sum of those rounded away from zero 5050

== places that are already enough ==
round(2.5d, 1)                     2.5
round(2.5d, 5)                     2.5
round(2.50d, 5)                    2.50
round(5d, 2)                       5
round(5i, 2)                       5

== the result scale is the number of places (or less) ==
round(1.23456d, 3)                 1.235
round(1.20000d, 3)                 1.200
round(9.999d, 2)                   10.00
round(0.001d, 2)                   0.00
round(-0.001d, 2)                  0.00

== floor, ceil and trunc (always scale 0) ==
2.7                                floor 2  ceil 3  trunc 2
2.2                                floor 2  ceil 3  trunc 2
2                                  floor 2  ceil 2  trunc 2
-2.2                               floor -3  ceil -2  trunc -2
-2.7                               floor -3  ceil -2  trunc -2
5.00                               floor 5  ceil 5  trunc 5
0.5                                floor 0  ceil 1  trunc 0
-0.5                               floor -1  ceil 0  trunc 0

== invalid arguments ==
round(1d, -1)                      error: invalid argument #2 to 'round' (number of places out of range [0, 28])
round(1d, 29)                      error: invalid argument #2 to 'round' (number of places out of range [0, 28])
round(1d, 1.5) truncates like other libs 1
round(1d, 0, 'bogus')              error: invalid argument #3 to 'round' (invalid rounding mode, expected 'halfeven', 'awayfromzero', 'tozero', 'tonegativeinfinity' or 'topositiveinfinity')
round(1d)                          error: missing argument #2 to 'round' (number expected)
round(1.5, 0)                      error: invalid argument #1 to 'round' (decimal expected, got number)
floor('x')                         error: invalid argument #1 to 'floor' (decimal expected, got string)
